note Exercism-style exercise "grains": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/grains
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note square n is the grains on square n (1 .. 64) of a chessboard when each square doubles the
note last, starting from 1; total is the grains on the whole board.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/grains
om2
fn square n ulong to ulong
ret shl ulong 1 sub n 1
end
fn total to ulong
ret not ulong 0
end
